/*******************************************************************************
                jigCorpus registry — JIT Igor minion corpus.

    Pure data, no actions (the unitTests pattern). Included by `jiquery`, which
    runs queries against it. NO Start()/stop() wrapper — this is a registry file,
    not an execution file. CANONICAL: this is the source-of-truth JIT Igor corpus.
    See docs/minion-corpus-format.md.

    ============================================================================
    RE-BAKED 2026-07-31 from the CONSOLIDATED docs (docs/jit.md = what is true,
    docs/jitDesign.md = settled premises + open work), NOT from the eight files
    they replaced. Previous bake was 2026-06-29 and every one of its six claims
    needed regrading — four demoted, one refuted, one kept. That ratio is the
    argument for re-baking rather than appending.
    ============================================================================

    ⚠ ADVERSARIAL ABSORPTION IS THE HOUSE RULE HERE, AND IT IS NOT GENERIC
    CAUTION. This domain is where causal claims went FIVE FOR FIVE WRONG. So:

      - A RUN grades `verified`. A SOURCE READ grades `inferred`, however
        mechanical, however often repeated. The census below is a total
        enumeration confirmed twice and it is STILL `inferred`, because the
        format's rule is bones-not-shape and a grep is not bones. That is
        deliberately conservative and it is the point.
      - REPRODUCTION PROVES THE SYMPTOM, NEVER THE CAUSE (bear-trap #18). Where
        a symptom is `verified` and its explanation is not, they are SPLIT INTO
        TWO CLAIMS — see unaryPopsCrash / unarySeedCause. A reader acting on the
        symptom is safe; a reader acting on the cause is on notice.
      - A HYPOTHESIS THAT SURVIVES NARROWING IS NOT THEREBY CONFIRMED
        (bear-trap #19's corollary). Every `inferred` claim below names the
        space that was searched, so the next reader can re-run the search
        instead of re-trusting the conclusion.
      - AN ABSENCE CLAIM NAMES WHERE IT LOOKED (`searched`), per corpus-format
        RULE 1.
      - An OPEN is not a claim with hedges (RULE 2). Opens live in `openItems`
        and say what they BLOCK and what settling would COST.
      - ⚠ NEW GRADE 2026-07-31: `acquitted-unexplained`, and it is DELIBERATELY
        DISTINCT FROM `refuted`. It means: the predicted symptom DOES NOT OCCUR
        under the prosecution's best case, measured -- but the mechanism that
        PROTECTS us is unestablished. Safe by measurement, not by understanding.
        A refuted claim is dead and needs no guard; an acquitted-unexplained one
        keeps a FIXTURE STANDING GUARD, because the day the protecting mechanism
        changes, the acquittal expires and nothing else would notice.

    THE ACCEPTANCE TEST this corpus must pass: an agent asked "does the JIT gIF
    branch work?" must NOT answer "yes, taken->99". It must say that was a
    shape-read, since refuted, and that the branch IS now genuinely gated per an
    IR dump while the RETURN VALUE is not merged. Both halves, or the format
    failed.
*******************************************************************************/
